error[E0277]: `MySet` cannot implement a sealed Verum trait
  --> tests/ui/compile_fail/cons_list_cannot_be_forged.rs:13:26
   |
13 | impl verum::ConsList for MySet {}
   |                          ^^^^^ not sealed by Verum
   |
   = help: the trait `verum::sealed::private::SealedConsList` is not implemented for `MySet`
   = note: Verum's sealed traits are implemented by Verum itself and by its derive macros. Writing the impl by hand grants something no declaration authorises, and nothing would report the difference.
note: required by a bound in `ConsList`
  --> src/typelevel.rs
   |
   | pub trait ConsList: private::SealedConsList {}
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `ConsList`
   = note: `ConsList` is a "sealed trait", because to implement it you also need to implement `verum::sealed::private::SealedConsList`, which is not accessible; this is usually done to force you to use one of the provided types that already implement it
   = help: the following types implement the trait:
             ()
             (H, T)
